## Start here

1. Open [[TODAY]] and record the unaided first model before consulting sources.
2. Attempt [[curriculum/BASELINE_DIAGNOSTIC|the baseline diagnostic]].
3. Follow [[tracking/{{WEEK_ID}}|the active weekly plan]].
4. Use [[curriculum/SKILL_MAP|the skill map]] to understand dependencies.
5. Read [[tracking/ROADMAP|the roadmap]] after preserving the initial diagnostic.

Do not mark anything complete in advance. A checkmark records performed work; a skill status records evidence.

## Success standard

This course is complete only when the learner can:

- explain the central models of {{TOPIC}} without notes;
- reproduce representative methods or performances under defined conditions;
- apply those methods independently to unfamiliar work;
- diagnose mistakes using recorded evidence; and
- produce and defend an integrated capstone or final assessment.

The exact capstone and acceptance criteria are defined during Phase 0 rather than assumed here.

## Operating loop

`diagnose → plan → attempt → preserve evidence → review → retrieve → adapt`

